\c 7
\s1 Elisha’s Prophecy of Plenty
\p \v 1 \w Then Elisha|strong="H477"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Hear|strong="H8085"\w* \w the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*! \w This is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w says|strong="H559"\w*: ‘\w About this time|strong="H6256"\w* \w tomorrow|strong="H4279"\w* \w at the gate|strong="H8179"\w* \w of Samaria|strong="H8111"\w*, \w a seah|strong="H5429"\w* \w of fine flour|strong="H5560"\w*\f + \fr 7:1 \fqa A seah \ft is approximately 6.6 dry quarts or 7.3 liters (probably about 8.2 pounds or 3.7 kilograms of flour); here and in verses 16 and 18.\f* \w will sell for a shekel|strong="H8255"\w*,\f + \fr 7:1 \fqa A shekel \ft is approximately 0.4 ounces or 11.4 grams, probably of silver; here and in verses 16 and 18.\f* \w and two seahs|strong="H5429"\w* \w of barley|strong="H8184"\w*\f + \fr 7:1 \fqa 2 seahs \ft is approximately 13.2 dry quarts or 14.6 liters (probably about 19.3 pounds or 8.8 kilograms of barley); here and in verses 16 and 18.\f* \w will sell for a shekel|strong="H8255"\w*.’”
\p \v 2 \w But the officer|strong="H7991"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w whose arm|strong="H3027"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w leaned|strong="H8172"\w* \w answered|strong="H6030"\w* \w the man|strong="H376"\w* \w of God|strong="H430"\w*, “\w Look|strong="H2009"\w*, \w even if the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w were to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w windows|strong="H699"\w* \w in heaven|strong="H8064"\w*, \w could this|strong="H2088"\w* \w really happen|strong="H1961"\w*?”
