\p \w So Samaria|strong="H8111"\w* \w was captured|strong="H3920"\w* \w in the sixth|strong="H8337"\w* \w year|strong="H8141"\w* \w of Hezekiah|strong="H2396"\w*, \w which|strong="H1931"\w* \w was the ninth|strong="H8672"\w* \w year|strong="H8141"\w* \w of Hoshea|strong="H1954"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*. \v 11 \w The king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Assyria|strong="H804"\w* \w exiled|strong="H1540"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H3478"\w* \w to Assyria|strong="H804"\w* \w and settled them|strong="H5148"\w* \w in Halah|strong="H2477"\w*, \w in Gozan|strong="H1470"\w* \w by the Habor|strong="H2249"\w* \w River|strong="H5104"\w*, \w and in the cities|strong="H5892"\w* \w of the Medes|strong="H4074"\w*. \v 12 \w This happened because|strong="H5921"\w* \w they did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w listen|strong="H8085"\w* \w to the voice|strong="H6963"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w their God|strong="H430"\w*, \w but violated|strong="H5674"\w* \w His covenant|strong="H1285"\w*— \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w the servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w had commanded|strong="H6680"\w* — \w and would neither|strong="H3808"\w* \w listen|strong="H8085"\w* \w nor|strong="H3808"\w* \w obey|strong="H6213"\w*.
