\p \v 13 \w In the fourteenth|strong="H702"\w* \w year|strong="H8141"\w* \w of Hezekiah’s|strong="H2396"\w* \w reign|strong="H4428"\w*, \w Sennacherib|strong="H5576"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Assyria|strong="H804"\w* \w attacked|strong="H5927"\w* \w and captured|strong="H8610"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the fortified|strong="H1219"\w* \w cities|strong="H5892"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*. \v 14 \w So Hezekiah|strong="H2396"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w word to|strong="H413"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Assyria|strong="H804"\w* \w at Lachish|strong="H3923"\w*, \w saying|strong="H559"\w*, “\w I have done wrong|strong="H2398"\w*; \w withdraw|strong="H7725"\w* \w from me|strong="H5921"\w*, \w and I will pay|strong="H5375"\w* \w whatever|strong="H834"\w* \w you demand|strong="H5414"\w* \w from me|strong="H5921"\w*.”
