\p \v 17 \w Nevertheless, the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Assyria|strong="H804"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w the Tartan|strong="H8661"\w*,\f + \fr 18:17 \ft Hebrew \fqa Tartan \ft is the title of a field marshal, general, or commander in the Assyrian military.\f* \w the Rabsaris|strong="H7249"\w*,\f + \fr 18:17 \ft Hebrew \fqa Rabsaris \ft is the title of the chief eunuch in the Assyrian military.\f* \w and the Rabshakeh|strong="H7262"\w*,\f + \fr 18:17 \ft Hebrew \fqa Rabshakeh \ft is the title of a high-ranking Assyrian military officer; here and throughout chapters 18 and 19, as well as Isaiah 36 and 37.\f* \w along with a great army|strong="H3515"\w*, \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w Lachish|strong="H3923"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Hezekiah|strong="H2396"\w* \w at Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*. \w They advanced up|strong="H5927"\w* \w to Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w and stationed themselves|strong="H5975"\w* \w by the aqueduct|strong="H8585"\w* \w of the upper|strong="H5945"\w* \w pool|strong="H1295"\w*, \w on the road|strong="H4546"\w* \w to the Launderer’s|strong="H3526"\w* \w Field|strong="H7704"\w*. \v 18 \w Then they called|strong="H7121"\w* \w for|strong="H413"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*. \w And Eliakim|strong="H471"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Hilkiah|strong="H2518"\w* \w the palace|strong="H1004"\w* \w administrator|strong="H5921"\w*, \w Shebnah|strong="H7644"\w* \w the scribe|strong="H5608"\w*, \w and Joah|strong="H3098"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Asaph|strong="H623"\w* \w the recorder|strong="H2142"\w*, \w went out|strong="H3318"\w* \w to them|strong="H413"\w*.
\p \v 19 \w The Rabshakeh|strong="H7262"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to them|strong="H413"\w*, “\w Tell|strong="H559"\w* \w Hezekiah|strong="H2396"\w* \w that this is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the great|strong="H1419"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w*, \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Assyria|strong="H804"\w*, \w says|strong="H559"\w*: \w What|strong="H4100"\w* \w is the basis|strong="H982"\w* \w of this|strong="H2088"\w* \w confidence|strong="H986"\w* \w of yours|strong="H834"\w*? \v 20 \w You claim|strong="H559"\w* \w to have a strategy|strong="H6098"\w* \w and strength|strong="H1369"\w* \w for war|strong="H4421"\w*, \w but|strong="H389"\w* \w these are empty|strong="H8193"\w* \w words|strong="H1697"\w*. \w In|strong="H5921"\w* \w whom|strong="H4310"\w* \w are you now|strong="H6258"\w* \w trusting|strong="H982"\w*, \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w you have rebelled|strong="H4775"\w* against me?
